text":"Referred to the Committee on the Judiciary, and in addition to the Committee on House Administration, for a period to be subsequently determined by the Speaker, in each case for consideration of such provisions as fall within the jurisdiction of the committee concerned."},"number":"HRES 1539","policyArea":"Government Operations and Politics","ranked":false,"stage":"introduced","summary":"Affirms the House's commitment to defend the Fourteenth and Fifteenth Amendments and oppose voter intimidation, voter suppression, and election interference, while calling for restoration of voting rights protections and opposing documentary citizenship requirements for voter registration.","summarySource":"ai","title":"Affirming the commitment of the House of Representatives to defend the Fourteenth and Fifteenth Amendments to the Constitution and to oppose efforts to intimidate voters, suppress the vote, or interfere with free and fair elections.","type":"hres","url":"https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/house-resolution/1539"},{"bipartisan":true,"cosponsors":1,"crossPartyCosponsors":1,"id":"hr10355-119","introducedDate":"2026-09-14","latestAction":{"actionDate":"2026-09-16","text":"Ordered to be Reported by the Yeas and Nays: 23 - 0."},"number":"HR 10355","policyArea":"Commerce","ranked":true,"stage":"introduced","summary":"The Small Business Administration must establish procedures within 180 days to ensure disaster loan outreach materials from all field operations centers consistently contain accurate, current information about disaster loan program terms, eligibility processes, and other relevant details, including standardized templates and annual consistency reviews.","summarySource":"ai","title":"Disaster Loan Outreach Consistency Act","type":"hr","url":"https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/house-bill/10355"},{"bipartisan":false,"cosponsors":0,"crossPartyCosponsors":0,"id":"hr10343-119","introducedDate":"2026-09-10","latestAction":{"actionDate":"2026-09-10","text":"Referred to the Committee on Small Business, and in addition to the Committee on Science, Space, and Technology, for a period to be subsequently determined by the Speaker, in each case for consideration of such provisions as fall within the jurisdiction of the committee concerned."},"number":"HR 10343","policyArea":"Commerce","ranked":true,"stage":"introduced","summary":"The bill amends the Small Business Act to require Federal agencies to provide enhanced debriefing materials to small businesses denied Small Business Innovation Research (SBIR) or Small Business Technology Transfer (STTR) awards. The debriefing must include evaluation of proposal deficiencies, proposal ranking, and denial rationale, with opportunities for follow-up questions.","summarySource":"ai","title":"CLEAR Feedback Act","type":"hr","url":"https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/house-bill/10343"},{"bipartisan":false,"cosponsors":0,"crossPartyCosponsors":0,"id":"hr10344-119","introducedDate":"2026-09-10","latestAction":{"actionDate":"2026-09-10","text":"Referred to the House Committee on Ways and Means."},"number":"HR 10344","policyArea":"Taxation","ranked":true,"stage":"introduced","summary":"The bill would amend the Internal Revenue Code to allow the IRS to disclose taxpayer return information to the Small Business Administration upon written request for purposes of determining eligibility for disaster loans under the Small Business Act.","summarySource":"ai","title":"Fast Track Disaster Relief Act","type":"hr","url":"https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/house-bill/10344"}],"state":"NJ","topCrossPartyCollaborators":[{"bioguideId":"F000466","caucus":"R","count":3,"name":"Brian K. Fitzpatrick"},{"bioguideId":"B001260","caucus":"R","count":2,"name":"Vern Buchanan"},{"bioguideId":"L000599","caucus":"R","count":2,"name":"Michael Lawler"},{"bioguideId":"K000404","caucus":"R","count":1,"name":"Kimberlyn King-Hinds"},{"bioguideId":"B001257","caucus":"R","count":1,"name":"Gus M. Bilirakis"}]}
